  "question": {
    "text": "The mass and the diameter of a planet are three times of the respective values for the earth. If the time period of oscillation of a simple pendulum on earth is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>,&nbsp;then the time period of oscillation of the same pendulum on the surface of the given planet would be",
    "image": null
  },
